WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:16.641
Uh-oh! Who are you?

2
00:00:16.642 --> 00:00:20.581
I'm a rattlesnake.

3
00:00:20.582 --> 00:00:24.866
Rattlesnakes are reptiles.

4
00:00:24.867 --> 00:00:27.515
Where do you live?

5
00:00:27.516 --> 00:00:32.452
Rattlesnakes live in North and South America.

6
00:00:32.453 --> 00:00:37.627
We live in prairies, forests, and deserts.

7
00:00:37.628 --> 00:00:40.803
What's on your tail?

8
00:00:40.804 --> 00:00:44.063
That's my rattle.

9
00:00:44.064 --> 00:00:51.718
We shake our rattles to warn enemies.

10
00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:54.716
What do you eat?

11
00:00:54.717 --> 00:00:59.023
We mostly eat small animals.

12
00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:04.534
We love rabbits, mice, and prairie dogs!

13
00:01:04.535 --> 00:01:07.641
How do you find food?

14
00:01:07.642 --> 00:01:13.052
Our tongues are shaped like forks.

15
00:01:13.053 --> 00:01:17.048
They help us smell prey.

16
00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:22.617
We can sense heat from prey too.

17
00:01:22.618 --> 00:01:26.218
You have big fangs!

18
00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:31.051
We use our fangs to bite.

19
00:01:31.052 --> 00:01:35.348
The bite kills our prey.

20
00:01:35.349 --> 00:01:39.481
Then we swallow the animal whole!

21
00:01:39.482 --> 00:01:43.140
Do rattlesnakes shed their skin?

22
00:01:43.141 --> 00:01:47.923
Yes, we shed our skin as we grow.

23
00:01:47.924 --> 00:01:52.359
We rub against rocks to loosen it.

24
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:56.476
Then we crawl right out of our skin!

25
00:01:56.477 --> 00:01:58.836
Good-bye.

26
00:01:58.837 --> 00:02:05.452
Good-bye, Rattlesnake!
